## 12. N-Queens

Another famous backtracking problem is **N-Queens**.

The goal is to place `N` queens on an `N × N` chessboard so that no two queens attack each other.

For example, with `4 × 4`:

```text
. Q . .
. . . Q
Q . . .
. . Q .
```

A queen cannot share the same:

```text
row
column
diagonal
```

Backtracking tries a position, checks whether it is safe, and if necessary removes the queen and tries another position.

---

## 13. N-Queens Pattern

The basic idea is:

```text
Place queen
    ↓
Check if safe
    ↓
Continue to next row
    ↓
If invalid → remove queen
    ↓
Try another position
```

This is the same fundamental pattern:

```text
Choose → Explore → Undo
```

---

## 14. Sudoku

Sudoku can also be solved using backtracking.

At an empty cell:

```text
Try a number
     ↓
Check if valid
     ↓
Place number
     ↓
Move to next empty cell
     ↓
If invalid → remove number
     ↓
Try another number
```

Again:

```text
Choose → Explore → Undo
```

